---
import PageLayout from "../../layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import Button from "../../components/shared/Button.astro";
import Badge from "../../components/shared/Badge.astro";

const box =
  "w-full font-mono text-xs p-3 rounded-lg border border-surface-300 dark:border-surface-700 bg-surface-50 dark:bg-surface-950 text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100";
const field =
  "mt-1 w-full px-3 py-2 rounded-lg border border-surface-300 dark:border-surface-700 bg-surface-50 dark:bg-surface-950 text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100";
const label = "block text-sm text-surface-700 dark:text-surface-300";
const card =
  "mb-6 p-6 rounded-xl bg-white dark:bg-surface-900 border border-surface-200 dark:border-surface-800";
const toggle = "inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-medium text-surface-800 dark:text-surface-200";
const demoBtn =
  "inline-flex items-center gap-2 font-medium rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-sm bg-surface-100 text-surface-800 hover:bg-surface-200 dark:bg-surface-800 dark:text-surface-200 dark:hover:bg-surface-700 transition-all";
---

<PageLayout
  title="SEMinR in the browser — PLS-SEM estimation — Nicholas P. Danks"
  description="Estimate, bootstrap, and assess a PLS-SEM model from SEMinR code and your own data, entirely in your browser: reliability, HTMT, path coefficients, mediation, PLSpredict, CVPAT, the congruence test, and a downloadable report. Your data never leaves your browser."
>
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16 sm:py-20">
    <header class="mb-8">
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 mb-4">
        <Badge label="Web App" variant="primary" />
        <Badge label="Runs on your computer" variant="accent" />
        <Badge label="No upload" variant="neutral" />
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-50 mb-4">
        SEMinR in the browser
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-surface-600 dark:text-surface-400 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
        Paste the SEMinR model you would run in R and your indicator data. The page
        estimates the PLS-SEM model, bootstraps it, runs PLSpredict, CVPAT and the
        congruence test, checks every result against the textbook thresholds, draws the
        path diagram, and gives you a report, the numbers, and the R script to reproduce
        it all. No R, no install.
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Demos -->
    <section class="mb-4 p-4 rounded-xl border border-surface-200 dark:border-surface-800 bg-white dark:bg-surface-900 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3" aria-label="Textbook demos">
      <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100">Try a textbook demo:</span>
      <button type="button" data-demo="corp-rep" class={demoBtn}>Corporate reputation</button>
      <button type="button" data-demo="moderation" class={demoBtn}>Moderation (CUSA × SC)</button>
      <span class="text-xs text-surface-500 dark:text-surface-400">Fills in the data and the model below; then press &ldquo;Run the full analysis&rdquo;. Or paste your own.</span>
    </section>

    <!-- Privacy -->
    <section class="mb-8 px-4 py-3 rounded-xl border border-accent-200 dark:border-accent-800 bg-accent-50/50 dark:bg-accent-900/20 text-sm text-surface-700 dark:text-surface-300 leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        <strong class="text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100">Your data never leaves your computer.</strong>
        Estimation, every bootstrap resample and every cross-validation fold run in your
        browser, on your own processor. No upload, no server, no account, no logging.
      </p>
      <details class="mt-1">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer text-accent-700 dark:text-accent-400">What the page can and cannot send</summary>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Apart from loading its own code from this site, the page makes two kinds of
          request, and only when you ask for them: the bundled demo dataset, when you press
          a demo button, and the optional Gemini review, which receives aggregate statistics
          and column <em>names</em>, never rows (the exact text is under &ldquo;What leaves
          the browser&rdquo; once you have run a model). Nothing you paste is sent anywhere
          else. Disconnect from the internet after the page has loaded and the analysis
          still works.
        </p>
      </details>
    </section>

    <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
      <section class={card + " lg:mb-0"}>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-2">
          <span class="text-accent-600 dark:text-accent-400">1.</span> Indicator data
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-surface-600 dark:text-surface-400 mb-3">
          One column per item with a header row of item names, one row per case.
          Comma-, semicolon- or tab-separated, so pasting from Excel, SPSS or SmartPLS
          works. Extra columns are ignored.
        </p>
        <textarea id="data" rows="12" spellcheck="false" class={box}
          placeholder={"comp_1,comp_2,comp_3,like_1,…\n5,6,5,7,…"}></textarea>
        <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
          <label class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-medium rounded-lg px-3 py-1.5 bg-surface-100 text-surface-800 hover:bg-surface-200 dark:bg-surface-800 dark:text-surface-200 dark:hover:bg-surface-700 cursor-pointer">
            <input id="file" type="file" accept=".csv,.tsv,.txt,text/csv,text/plain" class="sr-only" />
            Open a file…
          </label>
          <span class="text-xs text-surface-500 dark:text-surface-400">Read locally; never uploaded.</span>
        </div>
        <p id="data-status" class="text-xs mt-2 text-surface-500 dark:text-surface-400"></p>
      </section>

      <section class={card + " lg:mb-0"}>
        <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-2">
          <span class="text-accent-600 dark:text-accent-400">2.</span> SEMinR model
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-surface-600 dark:text-surface-400 mb-3">
          The same code you would run in R: <code>constructs()</code> with
          <code>composite()</code>, <code>reflective()</code>,
          <code>higher_composite()</code>, <code>interaction_term()</code> and
          <code>quadratic_term()</code>; <code>relationships()</code> with
          <code>paths()</code>. Assignments, comments and other lines are ignored.
        </p>
        <textarea id="code" rows="12" spellcheck="false" class={box}
          placeholder={'mm <- constructs(\n  composite("COMP", multi_items("comp_", 1:3)),\n  composite("QUAL", multi_items("qual_", 1:8), weights = mode_B),\n  composite("CUSA", single_item("cusa")))\n\nsm <- relationships(\n  paths(from = "QUAL", to = "COMP"),\n  paths(from = "COMP", to = "CUSA"))'}></textarea>
        <p id="code-status" class="text-xs mt-2 text-surface-500 dark:text-surface-400"></p>
      </section>
    </div>

    <!-- Options -->
    <section class={card + " mt-6"}>
      <details id="advanced">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-3 gap-y-1">
          <span class="text-lg font-semibold text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100">
            <span class="text-accent-600 dark:text-accent-400">3.</span> Options
          </span>
          <span id="options-summary" class="text-xs text-surface-500 dark:text-surface-400"></span>
          <span class="text-xs text-accent-600 dark:text-accent-400 ml-auto">change</span>
        </summary>

        <div class="mt-5 grid sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
          <label class={label}>Missing-value code
            <input id="missing-value" type="text" value="-99" class={field} placeholder="e.g. -99 (blank = none)" />
          </label>
          <label class={label}>Missing data
            <select id="missing" class={field}>
              <option value="mean_replacement">Mean replacement</option>
              <option value="na_omit">Drop incomplete cases</option>
            </select>
          </label>
          <label class={label}>Inner weighting scheme
            <select id="inner-weights" class={field}>
              <option value="path_weighting">Path weighting</option>
              <option value="path_factorial">Factorial</option>
            </select>
          </label>
          <label class={label}>Random seed
            <input id="seed" type="number" value="123" min="1" class={field} />
          </label>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-6 grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
          <div class="p-4 rounded-lg border border-surface-200 dark:border-surface-800">
            <label class={toggle}><input id="boot-enabled" type="checkbox" checked /> Bootstrap</label>
            <div class="mt-3 grid grid-cols-2 gap-3">
              <label class={label}>Resamples
                <input id="nboot" type="number" value="2000" min="50" max="10000" step="100" class={field} />
              </label>
              <label class={label}>Alpha
                <input id="alpha" type="number" value="0.05" min="0.001" max="0.5" step="0.01" class={field} />
              </label>
            </div>
            <p class="text-xs mt-2 text-surface-500 dark:text-surface-400">
              Percentile intervals for paths, loadings, weights, HTMT, total and indirect
              effects. Runs on all your cores; the congruence test reuses these resamples.
              Use 10,000 for the numbers you publish.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-4 rounded-lg border border-surface-200 dark:border-surface-800">
            <label class={toggle}><input id="predict-enabled" type="checkbox" checked /> PLSpredict</label>
            <div class="mt-3 grid grid-cols-2 gap-3">
              <label class={label}>Folds
                <input id="folds" type="number" value="10" min="2" max="50" class={field} />
              </label>
              <label class={label}>Scheme
                <select id="technique" class={field}>
                  <option value="predict_DA">Direct antecedents</option>
                  <option value="predict_EA">Earliest antecedents</option>
                </select>
              </label>
            </div>
            <label class={label + " mt-3"}>Key target construct
              <select id="key-target" class={field}>
                <option value="auto">Automatic (final outcome)</option>
              </select>
            </label>
            <label class={toggle + " mt-3"}><input id="cvpat-enabled" type="checkbox" checked /> CVPAT</label>
            <label class={label + " mt-2"}>CVPAT resamples
              <input id="cvpat-nboot" type="number" value="1000" min="50" max="5000" step="100" class={field} />
            </label>
          </div>

          <div class="p-4 rounded-lg border border-surface-200 dark:border-surface-800">
            <label class={toggle}><input id="congruence-enabled" type="checkbox" checked /> Congruence test</label>
            <div class="mt-3 grid grid-cols-2 gap-3">
              <label class={label}>Resamples
                <input id="congruence-nboot" type="number" value="1000" min="50" max="10000" step="100" class={field} />
              </label>
              <label class={label}>Threshold
                <input id="congruence-threshold" type="number" value="1" min="0.5" max="1" step="0.05" class={field} />
              </label>
            </div>
            <div class="mt-3 text-sm">
              <span class="text-surface-700 dark:text-surface-300">Matrix diagonal</span>
              <div class="mt-1 flex flex-wrap gap-4">
                <label class="inline-flex items-center gap-2">
                  <input type="radio" name="diagonal" value="rhoA" checked />
                  <span>rho<sub>A</sub></span>
                </label>
                <label class="inline-flex items-center gap-2">
                  <input type="radio" name="diagonal" value="rhoC" />
                  <span>rho<sub>C</sub> <span class="text-surface-500 dark:text-surface-400">(as <code>congruence_test()</code>)</span></span>
                </label>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>
    </section>

    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 mb-4">
      <button id="run" type="button"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 font-semibold rounded-lg px-6 py-3 text-base bg-accent-700 text-white hover:bg-accent-800 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-all disabled:opacity-50">
        Run the full analysis
      </button>
      <button id="quick" type="button" title="Estimate and assess the measurement model only; takes under a second"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 font-semibold rounded-lg px-4 py-3 text-sm bg-surface-100 text-surface-800 hover:bg-surface-200 dark:bg-surface-800 dark:text-surface-200 dark:hover:bg-surface-700 transition-all disabled:opacity-50">
        Quick look
      </button>
      <button id="cancel" type="button"
        class="hidden [&:not(.hidden)]:inline-flex items-center gap-2 font-medium rounded-lg px-4 py-3 text-sm text-surface-600 dark:text-surface-400 hover:text-red-600">
        Cancel
      </button>
      <span id="elapsed" class="text-xs text-surface-500 dark:text-surface-400"></span>
    </div>

    <div id="progress-wrap" class="hidden mb-8 p-4 rounded-lg border border-surface-200 dark:border-surface-800 bg-white dark:bg-surface-900">
      <ul id="stages" class="space-y-1 text-sm"></ul>
    </div>

    <div id="error" class="hidden mb-8 p-4 rounded-lg border border-red-300 dark:border-red-800 bg-red-50 dark:bg-red-900/20 text-sm text-red-800 dark:text-red-200 whitespace-pre-wrap"></div>

    <section id="results" class="hidden">
      <div class="sticky top-16 z-30 -mx-4 px-4 py-1.5 glass flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1">
        <nav id="results-nav" class="flex items-center max-sm:w-full max-sm:overflow-x-auto sm:flex-wrap" aria-label="Results sections"></nav>
        <div class="ml-auto flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5">
          <button id="download-html" type="button" class="text-xs font-semibold rounded-md px-2.5 py-1 bg-accent-700 text-white hover:bg-accent-800">Download report</button>
          <button id="download-json" type="button" class="text-xs font-medium rounded-md px-2.5 py-1 bg-surface-100 text-surface-800 hover:bg-surface-200 dark:bg-surface-800 dark:text-surface-200 dark:hover:bg-surface-700">JSON</button>
          <button id="download-r" type="button" class="text-xs font-medium rounded-md px-2.5 py-1 bg-surface-100 text-surface-800 hover:bg-surface-200 dark:bg-surface-800 dark:text-surface-200 dark:hover:bg-surface-700">R script</button>
          <button id="download-svg" type="button" class="hidden text-xs font-medium rounded-md px-2.5 py-1 bg-surface-100 text-surface-800 hover:bg-surface-200 dark:bg-surface-800 dark:text-surface-200 dark:hover:bg-surface-700">Diagram SVG</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div id="results-summary" class="report"></div>

      <!-- Evaluation assistant -->
      <section id="evaluate" class="hidden scroll-mt-28 mt-10 mb-4 p-6 rounded-xl border border-accent-200 dark:border-accent-800 bg-accent-50/40 dark:bg-accent-900/10">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-50 mb-2">Ask Gemini to review this model</h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-surface-700 dark:text-surface-300 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mb-3">
          A Gemini model reads the aggregate results of this run, assesses them against the PLS-SEM
          literature, and tests the improvements it proposes by asking this page to
          re-estimate alternative specifications. Those runs happen here, in your browser,
          on your data; the model only ever receives aggregate statistics.
        </p>
        <ul class="text-sm text-surface-700 dark:text-surface-300 list-disc pl-5 mb-4 space-y-1 max-w-3xl">
          <li><strong>Your data never leaves your computer.</strong> What is sent is the digest under &ldquo;What leaves the browser&rdquo;: reliability, loadings, paths, intervals, verdicts and column <em>names</em>. No rows, scores or residuals exist in it.</li>
          <li><strong>Free to use.</strong> This page carries a Gemini key of its own on Google's free tier, so the review costs you nothing. Requests go from your browser straight to <code>generativelanguage.googleapis.com</code>; there is no server in between. The free tier lets Google use what is sent (the aggregate digest, never your data) to improve its products.</li>
          <li><strong>Or your own key.</strong> If the shared free-tier limit is busy, or you would rather the digest went through your own Google account, paste a <a href="https://aistudio.google.com/apikey" rel="noopener" class="underline">Gemini API key</a> of your own below. It is kept in this tab unless you tick &ldquo;remember on this device&rdquo;. On a billed project a full review costs a few cents at <a href="https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/pricing" rel="noopener" class="underline">Google's list prices</a>, and Google does not use the content.</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-end gap-3 mb-3">
          <label class="block text-sm text-surface-700 dark:text-surface-300">Model
            <select id="eval-model" class={field}>
              <option value="gemini-3.8-flash">Gemini 3.8 Flash (newest, fast)</option>
              <option value="gemini-3.6-flash">Gemini 3.6 Flash (fast)</option>
              <option value="gemini-pro-latest">Gemini Pro, latest (slower, more careful)</option>
            </select>
          </label>
          <p id="key-mode" class="text-sm text-surface-600 dark:text-surface-400 pb-2 hidden">Using this site's free key.</p>
        </div>

        <details id="own-key" class="mb-3">
          <summary class="cursor-pointer text-sm font-medium text-surface-800 dark:text-surface-200">Use your own Gemini API key instead</summary>
          <div class="flex flex-wrap items-end gap-3 mt-2">
            <label class="block text-sm text-surface-700 dark:text-surface-300 grow max-w-md">Gemini API key
              <input id="api-key" type="password" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" placeholder="AIza…" class={field} />
            </label>
            <label class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-surface-700 dark:text-surface-300 pb-2">
              <input id="remember-key" type="checkbox" /> remember on this device
            </label>
            <button id="eval-forget" type="button" class="text-xs text-surface-500 dark:text-surface-400 underline pb-2">forget key</button>
          </div>
        </details>

        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <button id="eval-start" type="button"
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 font-semibold rounded-lg px-5 py-2.5 text-sm bg-accent-700 text-white hover:bg-accent-800 shadow-sm disabled:opacity-50">
            Evaluate this model
          </button>
          <button id="eval-show-digest" type="button"
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 font-medium rounded-lg px-3 py-2 text-sm bg-surface-100 text-surface-800 hover:bg-surface-200 dark:bg-surface-800 dark:text-surface-200 dark:hover:bg-surface-700">
            What leaves the browser
          </button>
          <button id="eval-stop" type="button" class="hidden text-sm font-medium text-red-700 dark:text-red-300 underline">Stop</button>
          <span id="eval-status" class="text-xs text-surface-500 dark:text-surface-400"></span>
        </div>
        <div id="eval-working" class="hidden mb-3 [&:not(.hidden)]:flex items-center gap-3 p-3 rounded-lg border border-accent-300 dark:border-accent-700 bg-white dark:bg-surface-900 text-sm">
          <span class="inline-block w-4 h-4 rounded-full border-2 border-accent-600 border-t-transparent animate-spin" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <span class="phase font-medium text-surface-800 dark:text-surface-200">Working…</span>
          <span class="elapsed ml-auto font-mono text-xs text-surface-500 dark:text-surface-400"></span>
        </div>
        <pre id="eval-digest" class="hidden text-xs p-3 mb-3 rounded-lg border border-surface-300 dark:border-surface-700 bg-white dark:bg-surface-950 text-surface-800 dark:text-surface-200 max-h-96 overflow-auto whitespace-pre-wrap"></pre>

        <div id="eval-transcript" class="report space-y-4 mb-4"></div>

        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-end gap-3">
          <label class="block text-sm text-surface-700 dark:text-surface-300 grow">Question or follow-up (optional)
            <textarea id="eval-question" rows="2" class={box} placeholder="e.g. Is CUSA a defensible single-item construct here? Would a higher-order QUAL help?"></textarea>
          </label>
          <button id="eval-send" type="button"
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 font-medium rounded-lg px-4 py-2.5 text-sm bg-surface-100 text-surface-800 hover:bg-surface-200 dark:bg-surface-800 dark:text-surface-200 dark:hover:bg-surface-700 disabled:opacity-50">
            Send
          </button>
        </div>
        <p id="eval-usage" class="text-xs mt-2 text-surface-500 dark:text-surface-400"></p>
      </section>

      <div id="results-body" class="report"></div>
    </section>

    <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-surface-200 dark:border-surface-800">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-3">What is computed</h2>
      <ul class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-x-8 gap-y-1 text-sm text-surface-600 dark:text-surface-400 list-disc pl-5 mb-8">
        <li>PLS path modeling with mode A, mode B, unit-weight and PLSc (reflective) constructs, two-stage higher-order composites, interaction and quadratic terms</li>
        <li>Outer loadings and weights, Cronbach's alpha, rho<sub>A</sub>, rho<sub>C</sub>, AVE, indicator and antecedent VIFs</li>
        <li>HTMT with bootstrap intervals, Fornell&ndash;Larcker, cross-loadings</li>
        <li>Path coefficients, R&sup2;, f&sup2;, total, total indirect and specific indirect effects with percentile bootstrap intervals</li>
        <li>PLSpredict (k-fold, DA/EA) against the linear-model benchmark, Q&sup2;<sub>predict</sub>, and CVPAT</li>
        <li>The bootstrapped congruence-coefficient test (Franke, Sarstedt &amp; Danks, 2021)</li>
        <li>Threshold assessment following <em>PLS-SEM Using R</em>, with every rule and source stated</li>
        <li>Path diagrams as seminr's <code>plot()</code>, a standalone HTML report, all results as JSON, and the R script</li>
        <li>An optional review by a Gemini model (free on this site's key, or with your own) that sees aggregate results only and tests its suggestions by re-running models here</li>
      </ul>
      <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100 mb-2">How closely it matches R</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-surface-600 dark:text-surface-400 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mb-8">
        The engine is the open-source TypeScript port of SEMinR and seminrExtras.
        Point estimates, the summary tables and PLSpredict reproduce R exactly
        (PLSpredict includes R's fold shuffle for a given seed). The bootstrap uses
        R's random number generator too, but seminr draws its resamples on a
        parallel stream, so intervals agree with R to Monte Carlo error, not digit
        for digit. The congruence test with rho<sub>C</sub> is bit-identical to
        <code>seminrExtras::congruence_test()</code>.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <Button href="https://github.com/sem-in-r/seminr-ts" variant="secondary" external>seminr-ts on GitHub</Button>
        <Button href="https://github.com/sem-in-r/seminrExtras" variant="secondary" external>seminrExtras on GitHub</Button>
        <Button href="/learn" variant="secondary">Learn PLS-SEM</Button>
        <Button href="/software" variant="secondary">All software</Button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</PageLayout>

<script>
  import { mount } from "../../lib/seminr/app";
  mount();
</script>
